        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            The flake blend does more work than the base color underneath it — it's what actually hides the dust, tire marks, and daily grime that make a garage floor look old. For most garages, <strong class="text-white">Storm Gray with a black/white/gray blend at medium-to-full broadcast</strong> is the safe, correct default. Go cooler or more monochrome for a showroom garage, warmer or earth-toned for a dusty climate, and darker with a lighter accent scatter if you want real drama — just match the density to how hard the floor is actually going to work.
          </p>
